nger receives enough persistent snowfall to sustain them.[26]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AETH-BIB-Mount_Kenya-Kilimanjaroflug_1929-30-LBS_MH02-07-0275.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Ellesmere_Island_05.jpg/500px-Ellesmere_Island_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Ellesmere_Island_05.jpg/1280px-Ellesmere_Island_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Ellesmere_Island_05.jpg/500px-Ellesmere_Island_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The overhanging icefront of the advancing Webber Glacier with waterfalls (Borup Fiord area, Northern Ellesmere Island) on July 20, 1978. Debris rich layers have been sheared and folded into the basal cold glacier ice. The glacier front is 6 km broad and up to 40 m high","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEllesmere_Island_05.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Geirangerfjord_%286-2007%29.jpg/500px-Geirangerfjord_%286-2007%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Geirangerfjord_%286-2007%29.jpg/500px-Geirangerfjord_%286-2007%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Differential erosion enhances relief, as clear in this very steep-sided Norwegian fjord.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeirangerfjord_(6-2007).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/TitlisIceCracksDeep.jpg/500px-TitlisIceCracksDeep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/TitlisIceCracksDeep.jpg/1280px-TitlisIceCracksDeep.jpg?utm_sour